description:
## Best Case
If the array is already sorted, bubble sort with early exit only does ONE pass with zero swaps, then stops.

**Best case: O(n)** - just one pass to confirm it's sorted.

```cpp
// With early exit optimization:
do {
    swapped = false;
    for (int i = 0; i < n-1; i++) {
        if (arr[i] > arr[i+1]) {
            swap(arr[i], arr[i+1]);
            swapped = true;
        }
    }
} while (swapped);
```

## Worst Case
If the array is completely reversed (e.g. `[5,4,3,2,1]`), every element needs to bubble all the way across. Every pass, every comparison, every swap.

**Worst case: O(n²)**

